<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"> <head> <meta charset="utf-8"> <meta content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=yes" name="viewport"> <title>svg_rasterization</title> </head> <body> <main> <h1 id="sec:images">1 Per-image SVG rasterization</h1> <figure id="fig:vector"> <img alt="Figure 1 A vector figure retained as SVG." src="figure.svg"> <figcaption aria-hidden="true">Figure 1 A vector figure retained as SVG.</figcaption> </figure> <figure id="fig:raster"> <img alt="Figure 2 The same figure explicitly rasterized." data-to-png="true" src="figure.svg"> <figcaption aria-hidden="true">Figure 2 The same figure explicitly rasterized.</figcaption> </figure> <figure id="fig:scaled"> <img alt="Figure 3 The rasterized figure at twice the default scale." data-to-png="true" data-to-png-scale="2" src="figure.svg"> <figcaption aria-hidden="true">Figure 3 The rasterized figure at twice the default scale.</figcaption> </figure> <p>Compare Figure <a href="#fig:vector">1</a>, Figure <a href="#fig:raster">2</a>, and Figure <a href="#fig:scaled">3</a>. The image-level conversion options should affect only the selected DOCX images.</p> </main> </body> </html>
